# Dashboard build-time settings (Vite).
#
# Vite loads its environment from THIS directory, not from the repository root
# `.env`. Copy this file to `frontend/.env`, or set the variables in the shell
# that runs `npm run build`.
#
# Everything here is optional. The dashboard works with none of it set.

# ---- Backend location ----------------------------------------------------
# Only needed when the API is on a different origin from the dashboard. By
# default the dashboard uses relative URLs, which the dev server proxies and
# IIS or nginx proxies in production.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://amnp-api.example.com
# VITE_WS_URL=wss://amnp-api.example.com/ws/live

# ---- Virtual path --------------------------------------------------------
# Set when the dashboard is served from beneath the site root, e.g. an IIS
# application under Default Web Site. Must match the application alias exactly.
# See docs/deployment-iis.md.
# VITE_BASE_PATH=/MNS

# ---- Google basemap (optional) -------------------------------------------
# Enables the "Google map" tab on the navigation, fleet and demonstration
# charts: the same layers, legend and positions over Google's satellite
# imagery. It is a second view only - nothing on it feeds any estimator, and
# the platform chart in the first tab is drawn entirely from the platform's own
# data and is unaffected by this setting.
#
# The Google view needs the public internet and a billed Google Cloud key with
# the "Maps JavaScript API" enabled. Leave it unset on an isolated network: the
# tab then explains that it is not configured instead of showing a blank chart.
#
# Restrict the key to the dashboard's own origins (HTTP referrer restrictions)
# before using it anywhere but a workstation - a key shipped in a browser bundle
# is public by definition.
# VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
